{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Discovered from `d68f-4771-ebc1-4ee4`\n\n`d68f` made a `# mechanism-ok:` admission a two-way door: the marker's reason must open\nwith a SUNSET TICKET, and `check_no_open_sunset_marker` refuses to close that ticket while\nthe marker is still in the tree. Closing the sunset ticket is the project's statement that\nthe justification expired, so the close is blocked until the mechanism goes.\n\nThat rule is forward-only, and every admission already in the tree predates it.\n\n## The measured state\n\nMeasured against `origin/main` at `a115c2edacd`, using the ratchet's OWN admitted set --\n`python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check`, which reports\n`active=647 new=32 increased=0 stale=0` and prints one `admitted` line per key -- rather\nthan a text scan of the tree. The unit is the admitted `kind::name` KEY, because a key is\nwhat a marker admits. Several marker sites can admit one key, so counting sites overstates\nthe backlog; restricting the scan to `src`/`scripts`/`tests` understates it.\n\n**32 admitted keys name 16 distinct sunset tickets. All 16 are `closed`.**\n\n| Kind | Keys |\n|---|---|\n| `ci_gate` | 22 |\n| `test_helper` | 4 |\n| `env_var` | 3 |\n| `lock` | 2 |\n| `config_key` | 1 |\n\n| Sunset ticket | Status | Keys |\n|---|---|---|\n| `1e24-bfc0` ergophobic-harassed-peacock | closed | 14 |\n| `2041-75d6-2a2f-4be9` golden-convergent-boutu | closed | 2 |\n| `aa9e-3d35-fd3e-41ee` jaunty-pugnacious-stinkpot | closed | 2 |\n| `eebc-6aa1-e45b-4325` jaded-pugnacious-isopod | closed | 2 |\n| `4932-ea62-cf4f-451b` daemonic-entodermal-tuatara | closed | 1 |\n| `4cfc-2de2-747d-4388` friendless-alabaster-cub | closed | 1 |\n| `7f3d-ddc9-04d9-4861` nepotistic-sensitive-arcticwolf | closed | 1 |\n| `933f-e7d8-696a-4fbd` imperfect-crotchety-sponge | closed | 1 |\n| `985f-0ec5-a61c-46ee` rebuffable-pebbly-xenurine | closed | 1 |\n| `a68c-9633-248c-4b06` evileyed-nontoxic-urutu | closed | 1 |\n| `b939-bc68-1cb2-4ee9` citified-earth-cottontail | closed | 1 |\n| `bab8-eb45-4dc2-4f02` cybernetic-ferric-stallion | closed | 1 |\n| `bc25-1351-dd0e-4909` dreamlike-sylphy-tern | closed | 1 |\n| `d279-4cf9` disgusted-fretful-hare | closed | 1 |\n| `f5ac-391c-ec70-4fa9` stable-jobless-coot | closed | 1 |\n| `metaphoric-late-creature` (`7eaa-502b-3d0f-4b08`) | closed | 1 |\n\nEvery admitted key names a well-formed sunset ticket; zero are malformed.\n\nSo the admission grammar's teeth bite on exactly zero of the admissions that exist. Every\none of the 32 is in the state `d68f` set out to forbid -- an admitted mechanism whose\nretirement ticket is already closed, with nothing left to retire it and no check that\nnotices. `d68f`'s close precheck cannot reach them, because it only fires at the moment a\nsunset ticket closes, and these closed long before the grammar existed.\n\n### Correcting the first census\n\nAn earlier revision of this plan recorded \"24 marker sites naming 19 distinct sunset\ntickets\", harvested by text-scanning the tree for the marker string and keeping only hits\nunder `scripts/`, `src/` and `tests/`. Re-running that harvest at its own stated base SHA\n`eba93991965` returns 101 sites, so the 24 was never a count of the tree. It is replaced\nby the table above, and was wrong in three ways:\n\n- it counted marker SITES rather than admitted KEYS, which are not the same unit;\n- it omitted `.github/workflows/` and `infra/` entirely, and `1e24-bfc0` alone accounts\n  for 14 of the 32 admitted keys -- 44% of the backlog was invisible to it;\n- it listed tickets (`dcc3-75ee-26ce-4840`, `48bd-1c15-c3b0-4a99`, `1cef-7fbc`,\n  `c6ce-4d8d-1c12-47cc`, `d730-8a25`, `68a9-2a6c-d9aa-49ad`) whose marker sites the\n  detectors do not admit as keys, so they are not part of this backlog at all.\n\nThe acceptance criteria below ask for zero over the TREE, so a census narrower than the\nratchet's own would have failed this plan's own criterion at the end.\n\n## What is NOT the remedy\n\nAdding a lint-time check that fails when a marker's sunset ticket is closed would make the\nratchet read the store. `sunset_ticket`'s docstring (`src/rebar/_commands/sunset_markers.py:41-47`)\nstates why it does not: the lint-time ratchet runs in checkouts where the `tickets` ref\nneed not be fetched, so resolving an id there would add a dependency it does not have. A\nscan-time check is also a new `ci_gate` -- new mechanism installed to police mechanism,\nwhich is the inversion `6b48`'s tidying skill exists to stop. If a gate is wanted anyway,\nit is a separate idea for the operator, not part of this.\n\n## The remedy\n\nDischarge the backlog by hand, one admitted key at a time. For each of the 32, exactly one of:\n\n- **remove the mechanism** -- the justification expired with its ticket, which is what the\n  closed sunset ticket asserts; this is the preferred outcome and shrinks the baseline\n- **repoint the marker** at a live ticket that will retire it, so the two-way door has\n  something to close against\n- **record that the mechanism is permanent** and so was never a sunset case, repointing it\n  at a ticket that says so\n\nThe third is a real category. `src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py:78` admits\n`RefLockPushError`, which the marker itself notes is \"an error type, not a lock\" -- a\ndetector misclassification rather than an expiring justification. The 14 `1e24-bfc0` keys\nare a second likely instance: each is an in-job wait before retrying a Gerrit patchset\ncheckout, which keeps a transient transport fault from casting a false `Verified -1`.\nThose want a different disposition from a genuinely expired admission, and conflating them\nis how this backlog formed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Every one of the 32 admitted keys is dispositioned: removed, repointed at an open\n      ticket, or documented as a permanent non-sunset admission.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check`, read over its own `admitted`\n      output rather than a text scan, reports zero admitted keys whose sunset ticket is\n      `closed`. This is a one-off verification by the author, not a shipped check.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` passes, with any resulting shrink\n      drained via `--update-stale` in the same change.\n- [ ] No new `ci_gate`, `env_var`, `config_key` or other mechanism is added by this work.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Provider neutrality\n\nNo model, vendor or harness is involved; this is tree surgery and tracker reads. The\nratchet, the admission grammar and the close precheck are all in-process and read no CI\nenvironment, so the work behaves identically with any CI provider or none."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793744032574168001,"uuid":"7ff52e6a-67c1-4b1f-ba40-cd62e35fa227"}